Great game going. In months of on-and-off playing, this is the second
or third time I've really felt I could go all the way with my dwarven
archeologist. After a really rocky start (within 200 turns my pet had
died and I'd somehow managed to put on a -1 cursed helmet I could have
sworn was not cursed) I managed to achieve a few early victories. By
the time I walked into Medusa's level I had been crowned and had all
kinds of goodies, including some gray dragon scale mail (from a throne
wish), boots of speed, a helm of brilliance, cloak of magic
resistance, gauntlets of power, amulet of reflection, a couple of
magic markers, the list goes on. I also managed to have teleportitis
and teleport control, my first time with both. Dual-weilding Werebane
and a silver saber. The one thing I didn't have was a way to levitate,
so rather than take my chances with the various ; on Medusa's level
(even though my cloak was well-greased) I dug down to the castle,
squashed the army with the drawbridge, and claimed my steel wand. I
literally could not think of anything I wanted that I didn't already
have except for levitation, so I wished myself up a ring and stashed
the wand for emergencies.

I had been running around Burdended for a while because my main stash
was all the way back on DL8 next to a lawful altar. I had found
another one around DL18 so I decided to make a few trips down and set
up shop at a more convenient depth, bless a few Identify scrolls and
do as much identifying as possible before going into the Quest. Hiked
up to DL17, fell down the stairs with a chest, dropped most of my loot
into my new stash, then up to DL8 to retrieve all my old unidentified
stuff. To take as few trips as possible I was basically going to just
load everything I could into my bag of holding until I was burdened.
Figured it would be easier to throw everything in the bag first then
take out what I needed in my open inventory (two weapons, unicorn
horn, lizard corpse), so here I am on auto-pilot grabbing fistfulls of
stuff out of my large box and flinging it into my bag.

"As you put a wand of cancellation inside, you are blasted by a
magical explosion!"

ARGH.

The good news: the blast didn't kill me (not even close). I still have
all my intrinsics, my amulet, and all my good armor. I had a backup
luckstone and unicorn horn still in my box.

The bad news: My weapons were the first thing thrown in the bag, so no
more Werebane for me. The wand of wishing is gone having only used two
charges (including the scrolls of charging and ring of levitation I
used those charges on). A lot of replaceable items are gone, including
my entire stash of holy and unholy water and all my cursed scrolls of
teleportation.

I'm down but not out. I feel very lucky to have learned a valuable
lesson without actually dying. Having no other silver sabers at hand
and nothing else of note to use, I fell back on weilding my trusty +0
rusty thoroughly corroded pick-axe, did some sacrificing, and
eventually upgraded to Fire Brand. As far as I know Grayswandir hasn't
been generated in this game yet, so I might spend a few thousand turns
sacrificing for it before moving on. No more bag of holding, but my
old starting sack is probably still in the mines where I left it and
my gloves will still let me carry a great deal of gear. Izchak has a
lamp for me that might be magic, and there are some fountains around,
so I might luck into a wish to at least return my bag to me.

Going to lick my wounds and head into the quest with my head held high.


